WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.721
NVIDIA-based Linux AI systems commonly involve the NVIDIA driver, CUDA-related runtime libraries, and sometimes a CUDA toolkit.

00:00:08.721 --> 00:00:14.832
At a high level, the driver enables GPU operation and exposes capabilities to the system.

00:00:14.832 --> 00:00:21.493
The CUDA toolkit provides development tools and libraries used to build or run CUDA applications.

00:00:21.493 --> 00:00:24.995
These are related, but they are not the same thing.

00:00:24.995 --> 00:00:36.806
nvidia-smi is a common first check because it reports driver information, detected NVIDIA GPUs, utilization, memory use, temperature, power, and processes using the device.

00:00:36.806 --> 00:00:43.192
It is a useful signal, but it is not the final proof that a specific AI framework is working.

00:00:43.192 --> 00:00:53.973
A Python library, container, or inference runtime may still fail because of missing libraries, incompatible versions, or incorrect environment configuration.

00:00:53.973 --> 00:00:56.101
Compatibility planning matters.

00:00:56.101 --> 00:01:07.706
Driver versions, CUDA runtime libraries, cuDNN and related acceleration libraries, Python packages, containers, and inference runtimes may all have version expectations.

00:01:07.706 --> 00:01:14.916
Randomly mixing versions can create errors that look like model failures but are really stack mismatches.

00:01:14.916 --> 00:01:22.264
Stable AI systems benefit from known-good combinations rather than constant chasing of the newest packages.

00:01:22.264 --> 00:01:31.877
GPU visibility should be checked from the places that matter: the host shell, Python environment, container, notebook, and inference server.

00:01:31.877 --> 00:01:35.929
Each layer can have different visibility and library paths.

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:42.933
Document the driver version, runtime versions, container image, model runtime, and validation results.

00:01:42.933 --> 00:01:47.602
That documentation turns a working setup into something recoverable.
